      "dom_id": "step-q36443",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nI. $[1,2]\\cup [3,4]$\n\nII. $[0,1)$\n\nIII. $[0,1)\\cup (1,2]$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[1,2]\\cup [3,4]$ is closed. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $1,2,3,$ and $4.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not closed because:\n\n- $[0,1)$ has a boundary point $1$, which does not lie in the set.\n\n- $[0,1)\\cup (1,2]$ has a boundary point $1$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
