    "q-71799": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71799",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nI. $(-4,1)$\n\nII. $(2,4)\\cup (5,6)$\n\nIII. $(0,1)\\cup (7,9]$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-4,1)$ and $(2,4)\\cup (5,6)$ are open because:\n\n- The boundary points of the set $(-4,1)$ are $-4$, and $1.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of the set  $(2,4)\\cup (5,6)$ are $2$, $4$, $5$, and $6.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not open because $(0,1)\\cup (7,9]$ has four boundary points $0$, $1$, $7$, and $9$, and the point $9$ lies in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
