    "q-105201": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105201",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nI. $(2,5)$\n\nII. $(-3,0)\\cup (2,7)$\n\nIII. $(-2,2)\\cup (4,10]$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(2,5)$ and $(-3,0)\\cup (2,7)$ are open because:\n\n- The boundary points of the set $(2,5)$ are $2$, and $5.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of the set  $(-3,0)\\cup (2,7)$ are $-3$, $0$, $2$, and $7.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not open because $(-2,2)\\cup (4,10]$ has four boundary points $-2$, $2$, $4$, and $10$, and the point $10$ lies in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-105201-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and III only",
              "html": "I and III only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-105201-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "II and III only",
              "html": "II and III only"
            },
