    "q-65003": {
      "dom_id": "step-q65003",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nI. $(-\\infty ,1]$\n\nII. $(0,1)\\cup (5,6)$\n\nIII. $[-3,-1)\\cup (0,1]$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(0,1)\\cup (5,6)$ is open. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $0$, $1$, $5$, and $6.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $(-\\infty ,1]$ has a boundary point $1$ and it lies in the set.\n\n- $[-3,-1)\\cup (0,1]$ has four boundary points $-3$, $-1$, $0$, and $1$, and the points $-3$ and $1$ lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
