    "q-161638": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161638",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}\\le 3\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1<x<1,\\,0<y<2-{x}^{2}\\}$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
